From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kennytech73 <contact@bookworm-mon0.org>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 08:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: cix: amvx: forget sequence parameters on bitstream flush

Flushing the bitstream (input) port makes the decoder firmware drop the
sequence parameters it has parsed. The driver kept received_seq_param
set, so when the capture queue was started next, flush_and_qbufs() sent
an output flush to the running firmware, which rejects it:

  Firmware rsp: Error. code=3, message=V6/V8-H264DEC: Output flush only
  allowed when stopped, or after response _SEQUENCE_PARAMETERS.

STREAMON(CAPTURE) then failed with -EINVAL and the GStreamer v4l2 decoder
stopped producing frames. This happens when a player seeks while the
first source change is being handled, e.g. GNOME Showtime resuming a
video at its last position.

Clear received_seq_param when the input port is flushed, so the output
flush is only sent when the firmware accepts it.

Reproduced 3/3 with a flushing seek 10 ms after PAUSED (v4l2h264dec,
1080p H.264); fixed 3/3, later seeks unchanged.
---
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/cix/if/mvx_session.c b/drivers/media/platform/cix/if/mvx_session.c
index b0754b803f4d8b342855a893917d22ffb0a95e81..8affb2d9f69efac22e93c86329c7a1c572c27bea 100755
--- a/drivers/media/platform/cix/if/mvx_session.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/cix/if/mvx_session.c
@@ -4041,6 +4041,16 @@ int mvx_session_streamoff(struct mvx_session *session,
             if (dir == MVX_DIR_OUTPUT) {
                 port->hold_off_buffer_done = false;
                 port->in_port_changing = false;
+            } else {
+                /*
+                 * Flushing the bitstream port makes the firmware forget the
+                 * sequence parameters: it then refuses an output flush until
+                 * it has parsed them again ("Output flush only allowed when
+                 * stopped, or after response _SEQUENCE_PARAMETERS"). Without
+                 * this, a seek during the first source change (players that
+                 * resume at the last position) made STREAMON(CAPTURE) fail.
+                 */
+                session->port[MVX_DIR_OUTPUT].received_seq_param = false;
             }
         }
     }
